# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and applies these headers to every
# response it serves — see https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# This is an auth-gated dashboard with no first-party content worth indexing
# or embedding, so the policy below is deliberately strict: no framing, no
# unused browser APIs, a locked-down CSP.
#
# img-src allows blob: for the local preview of a photo picked for upload;
# media-src https: lets customers' Instagram videos/voice notes play.
#
# connect-src/img-src use `https:` (any HTTPS host) rather than a fixed
# domain because the backend API and R2 media host are only known via
# NUXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE / R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL at deploy time, not at build time
# of this file. Once you know your real api.yourbusiness.com and R2/CDN
# domains, replace `https:` in both directives with the exact host(s) —
# that's meaningfully tighter than any-HTTPS.
#
# script-src needs 'unsafe-inline': `npm run generate`'s output
# (`ssr:false`, static SPA) ships two small inline <script> tags — an
# importmap and the __NUXT__ hydration-config blob — and both embed a
# per-build hash/buildId, so a static sha256- allowlist here would break on
# every deploy. There's no v-html/innerHTML anywhere in this app (verified),
# so this doesn't open an obvious injection sink today; the fully-correct fix
# is a nonce-based CSP minted per-request, which needs an edge function (e.g.
# a Cloudflare Pages _worker.js) in front of the static output — worth doing
# if this ever needs to defend against a real XSS-injection surface.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; connect-src 'self' https:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
